--- body ---
## Context and author ruling

The original idea came from `conception/2026-11-01-dsh-superagent-ideas.md`
§ 1. PR #2214 already made an observe-only period one option in the design
note template and raid. On 2026-11-07 the author clarified: "I ask 1440 to
be a memo like in Workflow, so that it is up to the MOE to think and propose
the trial period for new behaviors."

This settles the earlier scope question. The deliverable is a short reminder
in `rules/workflow.md`, alongside the existing Imagine/Plan/Cycle guidance.
When proposing new autonomous behavior, MOE considers whether a trial would
be useful and, when appropriate, proposes its purpose and evaluation criteria.
The trial is proportionate to the proposal and remains MOE's judgment.

This replaces the original request for an author-picked global observe scope,
a formal "would have done" record convention and a mandatory positive-control
application. No blanket observe framework, fixed waiting period, automatic
constraint, new mechanism or required trial for every behavior is requested.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A concise reminder in `rules/workflow.md` says MOE considers a useful,
  proportionate trial when proposing new autonomous behavior and proposes its
  purpose and evaluation criteria when appropriate.
- [ ] Wording leaves that judgment with MOE; it introduces no mandatory trial,
  global observe convention, fixed waiting period or new mechanism.
